# SELinux suffix for bind mounts
# ONLY needed on SELinux-enabled systems (Fedora, RHEL, CentOS with SELinux enforcing)
# Most developers (Ubuntu, macOS, Windows, CI) should leave this EMPTY
#
# Default: Empty (no SELinux labeling - works for 95% of users)
# SELINUX_SUFFIX=

# If you're on a SELinux system (Fedora/RHEL), uncomment this:
# SELINUX_SUFFIX=:z,ro

